        "role": "user",
        "content": "Fictional rehearsal planning notes. These notes describe invented people and projects, not a real event.\n\n2026-10-26, 09:00, initial planning: Cedar is a short assistant demonstration. Its owner was initially Theo. The initial practice slot was Friday 2026-10-30 at 10:00, with a delivery checkpoint at 11:00 that day. Cedar's practice location had not been selected. The team planned to demonstrate conversational context, not a persistent personal memory store. The first draft suggested that the model might choose a practice venue, but that suggestion was explicitly rejected: a missing venue must remain unknown until someone confirms it.\n\n2026-10-26, 14:00, separate Maple planning: Maple is a different project, owned by Noah. Maple's practice is Friday 2026-10-30 at 09:00 in room Birch, and its delivery checkpoint is at 12:00. These are Maple's facts only. Maple's venue must not be used as Cedar's venue. Both projects use the same local clock. Maple's support volunteer is Mira, but a support role on Maple does not establish ownership of Cedar.\n\n2026-10-27, 11:00, accepted Cedar correction: Mira takes over as Cedar's owner from Theo. Theo remains a reviewer and will check the demo script. This is an actual ownership change, not merely a proposed substitution. Cedar's original practice and delivery times remain unchanged at this point. The team will prepare one short example showing that a later correction can replace an earlier fact. A forgotten detail should lead to an admission of uncertainty rather than an invented answer.\n\n2026-10-28, 15:00, accepted Cedar correction: move Cedar's practice from Friday at 10:00 to Friday 2026-10-30 at 10:30. Keep the date the same. The earlier 10:00 time is superseded. Move Cedar's delivery checkpoint from 11:00 to 11:15 on the same Friday. These are accepted changes. Cedar's owner is still Mira. A note proposing room Oak is only a suggestion: no location has been accepted or booked.\n\n2026-10-29, 16:00, final handover: no further changes were accepted for Cedar. The practice and delivery checkpoint are on the same day and clock. There is no booked or confirmed Cedar practice location in these notes. Do not infer one from Maple, the room Oak suggestion, or the rejected venue-selection idea. A later informal message asks whether Cedar could practice at 10:45, but the handover explicitly says that request is unconfirmed and does not change the accepted 10:30 slot. The owner remains Mira; Theo's review work does not reverse the ownership correction. Keep the final answer brief and structured so the receiving interface can check each field."
